From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:17:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] usb: musb: gadget: keep OUT packets that arrive before
 the next request

When an OUT request became the head of an idle endpoint,
musb_ep_restart() flushed the RX FIFO. A packet that the controller had
already ACKed into the FIFO while no request was queued was thrown away,
although the host considered it delivered. On the Galaxy A22 5G
(MT6833) large uploads over the NCM gadget stalled because of it.

Consume such a packet instead of flushing it. Queueing an OUT request
kicks a worker that runs musb_g_rx() for every OUT endpoint that has a
request and is not busy, so a completion never runs on the
usb_ep_queue() call stack. The worker takes a runtime PM reference,
keeps no request pointer across a giveback, and stops while the gadget
is unbound, stopped or suspended (gadget_callbacks, gadget_rx_started,
gadget_rx_paused, gadget_rx_resetting). musb_suspend() and the error and
remove paths cancel it before clocks or memory go away, musb_resume()
starts it again, and ep0 no longer calls back into a gadget driver that
is going away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
